# FODMAP Diet Weekly Planner

## Slide 1: Title Slide
- Title: FODMAP Diet Weekly Planner
- Subtitle: Your Guide to Managing IBS-D

---

## Slide 2: What is FODMAP?
- FODMAP stands for Fermentable Oligosaccharides, Disaccharides, Monosaccharides, and Polyols.
- These are short-chain carbohydrates that are poorly absorbed in the small intestine.
- Understanding FODMAP helps in managing digestive symptoms.

---

## Slide 3: App Features Overview
- User-friendly interface
- Customizable meal plans
- Integration with grocery delivery services
- Access to a rich recipe library

---

## Slide 4: Weekly Planner
- An interactive tool for planning meals throughout the week.
- Users can drag and drop meals to customize their plans.
- Weekly overview keeps track of dietary limits.

---

## Slide 5: Recipe Bank
- A diverse collection of FODMAP-friendly recipes.
- Categories include breakfast, lunch, dinner, and snacks.
- Nutritional information available for each recipe.

---

## Slide 6: Shopping List
- Automatically generated based on chosen meals.
- Option to edit and add non-FODMAP items.
- Integration with local grocery stores for online shopping.

---

## Slide 7: Symptom Journal
- Track symptoms related to FODMAP intake.
- Users can log symptoms daily and review patterns over time.
- Helpful for identifying trigger foods.

---

## Slide 8: Educational Resources
- Access to articles and research on the FODMAP diet.
- Tips for following the diet effectively.
- FAQ section to address common concerns.

---

## Slide 9: Technical Features
- Cross-platform compatibility (iOS, Android, Web)
- Offline functionality for meal planning on the go.
- Regular updates based on user feedback and new research.

---

## Slide 10: Benefits for IBS-D Patients
- Reduces digestive discomfort.
- Aids in identifying personal food triggers.
- Encourages a balanced, nutritious diet.
- Enhances overall quality of life for IBS-D sufferers.